From 9f94d44391546582e5b3f5543f51f2b96a644ba5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stefanoconiglio <33290924+stefanoconiglio@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 02:24:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 04/10] Editor commands to show the page in the editor:
 render-to, click-at, select

(render-to PATH W H) writes the page on display to PATH as a PNG fitted to W x H
pixels, again whenever it changes, and answers (page-image PATH PAGE COUNT W H); an
empty PATH stops it.  (click-at X Y) does what a click in the window does, from
pixels of that image: SyncTeX back to the source.  (select X0 Y0 X1 Y1) highlights
the text between two points on the image and answers (selected-text TEXT).  With
these an editor can show the page in a window of its own while TeXpresso runs with
no window (SDL offscreen driver).
---
 src/frontend/editor.c |  83 +++++++++++++++
 src/frontend/editor.h |  25 +++++
 src/frontend/main.c   | 238 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 346 insertions(+)

